    {
      "id": "commit:41d02f0",
      "node_type": "commit",
      "label": "Commit 41d02f0",
      "sha": "41d02f034725949f2b3d8bf30bf6b89f2ca08401",
      "short_sha": "41d02f0",
      "author": "Joakim T\u00f6rnqvist",
      "title": "Commit 41d02f0: TAPI - Consolidate ROADM node construction",
      "message": "GitHub Commit 41d02f0 by Joakim T\u00f6rnqvist (2026-08-13T12:56:29+00:00)\nRepository: opendaylight/transportpce\nMessage: TAPI - Consolidate ROADM node construction\n\nThe event-driven ROADM node builder TapiNetworkModelServiceImpl\nbuilds ROADM nodes for incremental topology updates, while\nConvertTopoORtoTapiAtInit builds them during bulk initialization.\nBoth paths previously maintained their own copy of the node-building\nlogic.\n\nMove that logic to\nORtoTapiTopoConversionTools#createRoadmTapiNode and make both callers\ndelegate to it. The update and initialization paths remain separate, but\nnow use the same implementation to populate node attributes and\nconstruct the node and inter-rule groups.\n\nThis also fixes the incremental path, which populated\nFixedLatencyCharacteristic with TapiConstants.COST_HOP_VALUE instead of\nFIXED_LATENCY_VALUE.\n\nJIRA: TRNSPRTPCE-979\nChange-Id: I63282c14e0fb1c4690ae66d47d717a2a6b6300f8\nSigned-off-by: Joakim T\u00f6rnqvist <joakim.tornqvist@smartoptics.com>\nLinked Jira Issues: TRNSPRTPCE-979\nModified Files: tapi/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/transportpce/tapi/topology/ConvertTopoORtoTapiAtInit.java, tapi/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/transportpce/tapi/topology/ORtoTapiTopoConversionTools.java, tapi/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/transportpce/tapi/topology/TapiNetworkModelServiceImpl.java",
      "timestamp": "2026-08-13T12:56:29+00:00",
      "url": "https://github.com/opendaylight/transportpce/commit/41d02f034725949f2b3d8bf30bf6b89f2ca08401",
      "project_id": "opendaylight/transportpce"
    },
    {
      "id": "commit:490a8fb",
      "node_type": "commit",
      "label": "Commit 490a8fb",
      "sha": "490a8fb04805d09e47113bc966fb6be4b1155aef",
      "short_sha": "490a8fb",
      "author": "Joakim T\u00f6rnqvist",
      "title": "Commit 490a8fb: TAPI - Guard createNep against null TP augs",
      "message": "GitHub Commit 490a8fb by Joakim T\u00f6rnqvist (2026-09-04T11:59:44+00:00)\nRepository: opendaylight/transportpce\nMessage: TAPI - Guard createNep against null TP augs\n\ncreateNep() dereferenced two OpenROADM termination point\naugmentations without checking they exist: the OTN-network-topology\nTerminationPoint1 (tp1) and the common-network TerminationPoint1\n(oorTpAug).\n\ntp1 is only present on xpdr client/network ports; a ROADM SRG or\ndegree TP going through this same method to build its OTS/OTSi NEP\nhas no such augmentation, so tp1.getTpSupportedInterfaces() threw an\nNPE and aborted the whole topology conversion. Guard on tp1 being\nnull in addition to the existing getTpSupportedInterfaces() == null\ncheck, and return an empty NEP list instead of null so it still\nmatches what every caller expects from onepList.addAll(...).\n\noorTpAug is expected to always be present, since every other read of\nthis augmentation in the class (in convertNode()) assumes as much,\nbut createNep() derives rate, port type and admin/operational state\nfrom it throughout the method. Bail out early with the same empty\nlist if it is ever missing, rather than leaving that assumption\nunchecked deep inside the method.\n\nAlso drop the now-redundant sicColl == null check: sicColl can no\nlonger be null once its Optional-defaulted assignment always\nproduces a (possibly empty) collection.\n\nJIRA: TRNSPRTPCE-996\nChange-Id: I49568163e26e61eeb30ed2ca3e3094d0c4b9e246\nSigned-off-by: Joakim T\u00f6rnqvist <joakim.tornqvist@smartoptics.com>\nLinked Jira Issues: TRNSPRTPCE-996\nModified Files: tapi/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/transportpce/tapi/topology/ORtoTapiTopoConversionTools.java",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-04T11:59:44+00:00",
      "url": "https://github.com/opendaylight/transportpce/commit/490a8fb04805d09e47113bc966fb6be4b1155aef",
      "project_id": "opendaylight/transportpce"
    },
